# Inference

Batch inference resolves the DEV `candidate` alias once per run or uses the supplied
numeric version. It scores only Gold rows without labels. Output includes observation
ID, series ID, origin time, label time, numeric inputs, prediction time, model name,
model version and source table. Labels are joined later by stable ID and label time.

The example appends prediction history. Retried runs can produce repeat predictions;
use `(id, label_time, model_version, predicted_at)` for event identity. Implement an
idempotent MERGE using a batch ID when business semantics require one prediction per
batch. The adapter intentionally bounds driver memory for this small reference.

Online serving and a REST API are extensions, with no extra scaffolding in the default
project. Before adding serving, use current AI Gateway-enabled inference tables and
verify cloud/region support; the legacy inference-table configuration is deprecated.
